# Build context exclusions.
#
# The build stage does `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here is uploaded to
# the daemon and baked into an image layer. Two things matter most:
#   1. Secrets: a developer `.env` is expected (docker-compose.yml uses env_file)
#      and would otherwise survive inside the build layer forever.
#   2. Size: node_modules/ and .git/ dominate the context and are rebuilt or
#      irrelevant inside the image.
#
# Do NOT exclude db/, src/, public/, package.json or tsconfig*.json: the build
# stage compiles src/, and the runtime stage copies db/ (migrations) and public/
# (the dashboard served from process.cwd()/public/dashboard).

# Secrets - never ship a local environment file into a layer.
.env
.env.*

# Dependencies and build output are produced inside the image.
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Version control and CI metadata.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Agent / tooling scratch directories.
.agents/
.atl/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Test and coverage material is not part of the runtime image.
test/
coverage/
artifacts/

# Documentation is not served by the runtime.
docs/
*.md

# Container definitions themselves never need to be inside the image.
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
compose.*.yml

# Logs and OS noise.
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*.tmp
*.temp
